// Rule 2: two states named Welcome. Nothing refers to Welcome (it is the initial state),
// so textX cannot notice the duplicate; a reference to it would have made textX report
// the problem first, with its own message. The second declaration is the culprit.
// A smaller machine than the ATM, because every state of the example ATM is referenced.
atm Kiosk

events touch, done

initial state Welcome "Touch the screen" {
    on touch -> Working
}

state Working "Please wait" {
    on done -> Working
}

state Welcome "Touch the screen" {
    on touch -> Working
}
